# GX-1: perform. FX held, the white keys: a beat repeat (the steps stay in their beat; let go, back where the
# song is), drops and solos (sequencers held silent), octaves, the fill; FX let go ends it all, and an FX
# used to perform rolls no new idea
wait 400
expect view 5
gx new breaks 2 1
tap PLAY
wait 1200
expect playing 1
expect step_lag 0
# W4 (a 16th): the drums sequencer stays on one step
press FX
key w3 down
wait 60
expect perf_rpt 1
wait 400
expect step_lag >1
key w3 up
wait 20
expect perf_rpt 0
wait 300
# back with the song
expect step_lag 0
# W2 (a beat) then W1 (half a bar): the last pressed wins; let go of it, the other is back
key w1 down
wait 30
key w0 down
wait 30
expect perf_rpt 8
key w0 up
wait 30
expect perf_rpt 4
key w1 up
# W5 drums only, W6 no drums, W10 an octave up, W9 + W10 two up, W11 the fill
key w4 down
wait 30
expect perf_mute 14
key w5 down
wait 30
expect perf_mute 15
key w4 up
key w5 up
key w9 down
wait 30
expect perf_oct 1
key w8 down
wait 30
expect perf_oct 2
key w10 down
wait 30
expect fill 1
expect playing 1
# FX let go with the keys still down: everything back, and no new idea
release FX
wait 100
expect perf_oct 0
expect perf_mute 0
expect perf_rpt 0
expect fill 0
key w8 up
key w9 up
key w10 up
wait 300
expect step_lag 0
expect playing 1
# FX tapped on its own is still a new idea (it comes in at the next bar, from bar 1)
tap FX
wait 2500
expect playing 1
tap PLAY
wait 300
expect playing 0
